<title>AUSTRALIA: AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - June 24.</title>
<headline>AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - June 24.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for June 24</p>
<p>In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	     AH	   PH 13 PCT    PH 14  PCT</p>
<p>    Jun    170.50 -8    179.00 -8    187.50 -4    200.00 -4</p>
<p>    Jul    167.50 -8    176.00 -8    184.50 -4    199.00 -4</p>
<p>    Aug    165.00 -6    174.50 -6    182.00 -3    198.00 -3</p>
<p>    Sept   166.00 -6    175.50 -6    182.00 -3    198.00 -3</p>
<p>    Oct    169.00 -6    177.50 -6    184.00 -3    199.00 -3</p>
<p>    Nov    170.00 -6    178.50 -6    185.50 -3    200.00 -3</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat fell A$1.00 per tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>    National FOB	170.00</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:  Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  145.50	    Port Adelaide	 147.00</p>
<p>    Gladstone     145.75	    Port Giles	    147.75</p>
<p>    Brisbane	143.50	    Wallaroo		145.50</p>
<p> New South Wales			Port Pirie	    142.50</p>
<p>    Newcastle     145.50	    Port Lincoln	  148.75</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   146.00	    Thevenard	     143.75</p>
<p> Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 145.00	     Esperance	    150.25</p>
<p>    Portland	146.00	     Albany		 151.25</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    153.25</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    151.25</p>
<p>AWB MARKET COMMENTARY: Prices continue to weaken in the U.S. as harvest progresses. French wheat prices also weaken in sympathy with U.S. values.</p>
<p>AWB cash bids for New South Wales A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>			 1996/97 crop		1997/98 crop</p>
<p>    ASW/APW	  A$174.00 Newcastle	A$156.00 Newcastle</p>
<p>    AH1:	     A$184.00 Newcastle	A$169.00 Newcastle</p>
<p>    PH 13:	   A$209.00 Newcastle	A$184.00 Newcastle</p>
<p>    Feed Barley    A$154.00 *State avge    A$125.00 *State avge</p>
<p>			 ex farm June/July	 ex farm Nov/Dec</p>
<p>    Sorghum	  A$156.00 Newcastle	No bid</p>
<p>			 Jul/Aug</p>
<p>    Triticale	A$158.00 *State avge    A$119.00 *ex farm</p>
<p>			 ex farm June/July	 Dec/Jan</p>
<p>NOTES: The multigrade indicator price represents the AWB's view of the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract fob price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered by the AWB.  </p>
<p>ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; PW = Premium White; Percentages = protein content.</p>
<p>* Prices vary between regions.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
